# The accessors of md_alg (D406: md_alg.ragged_row, md_alg.ragged_entry,
# md_alg.wrap, md_alg.grid_read) and the grid plan (D[md-alg-stages]) by
# themselves, on the host. Both lowerings take the code of their emitters,
# so a contract test of one against the other could not fail (review of
# #862); these are their values, worked out by hand from the formats of
# RaggedRows.h and the definitions in MDAlgOps.td, and those of the grid
# plan, min(max(floor(L / w), least), most) with the width from an
# occupancy, (occupancy / (n / V))^(1/3), where it is given.
#
# RUN: mdir-opt %S/Inputs/md-alg/accessors.mlir --convert-md-alg-to-scf \
# RUN: | mlir-opt %lower_loops_to_llvm \
# RUN: | mlir-runner -e main --entry-point-result=void \
# RUN:     --shared-libs=%mlir_c_runner_utils \
# RUN: | FileCheck %s
#
# Rows 0, 1, 2 of ragged rows of 3 rows of 2, 0, and 3 entries of 2 values:
# (first, count) = (5, 2), (9, 0), (9, 3); checked, row 2 the same, rows 3
# and 7 past the rows and any row of an empty buffer (0, 0).
# CHECK:      5
# CHECK-NEXT: 2
# CHECK-NEXT: 9
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 9
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: 9
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# Entries: row 0 entry 1 value 0, row 2 entry 1 value 1, row 2 entry 2
# value 0.
# CHECK-NEXT: 102
# CHECK-NEXT: 107
# CHECK-NEXT: 108
# Wraps: 3 + 4 in 10, 8 + 5 in 10, 9 + 9 in 10 compared signed, 0 + 0 in
# 1, and 6 + 7 in 10 as index.
# CHECK-NEXT: 7
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: 8
# CHECK-NEXT: 0
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# Grid reads: point 5 of f32, an inactive lane at the base (point 2),
# point 5 active, and point 5 of f64 by index.
# CHECK-NEXT: 5.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 2.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 5.5
# CHECK-NEXT: 5.25
# Grid plans: 30 / 7; 30 / 100 (the least); 1e9 (the most); a length and a
# width that are not numbers (the least); an infinite length and a width
# of 0 (the most); a negative length (the least); 10 / 5 with a least of 3.
# CHECK-NEXT: 4
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 256
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 256
# CHECK-NEXT: 256
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# By an occupancy of 64: 3,000 in a cube of 30 (an edge of 8.32), none (an
# infinite edge), 180,000 in 400 x 90 x 50 (an edge of 8.62); then 30 / 7
# in f32.
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: 3
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 1
# CHECK-NEXT: 46
# CHECK-NEXT: 10
# CHECK-NEXT: 4
